CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* moved out: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* move assignment: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] .* WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
g++ 13 (-fsanitize=address,undefined) and clang++ 18 accept this program,
and it fails only its WRONG assertion.  An implicitly declared copy
operation that would be deleted is left without a body (do_not_typechecked)
instead of being diagnosed when it is merely a candidate.
